;; Cyclic clusters of the module graph: which modules are tangled together, and under what name.
;; Every cluster is a strongly connected component, so no cut short of breaking the cycle removes a
;; module from one. A cluster keeps its name while it shrinks and splits.
;;
;; Membership is a ceiling. Adding a module to a cluster, merging two, or forming a new cycle fails;
;; shrinking, splitting and dissolving pass, and the shrink workflow records them on master.
;; `./bin/mage fix-module-cycles` writes this file and never widens it: that is a hand edit, and the
;; PR making it has to say why. :mode :observe reports the same changes without failing.
